  "finding": "A strict 1-for-1 trade, measured in BOTH orderings on the real authoritative gate.  Evict the crystal and route the supplies first: NFC_VDD_A and NFC_VDD_D both close (+2) and NFC_XIN and NFC_XOUT each come back one join short (-2), 73 -> 73.  Route the crystal first: it rebuilds COMPLETELY and better than it was (XIN 7.237 mm, XOUT 4.947 mm, zero vias) and both supplies return to NO_LEGAL_ESCAPE_DST at U9.3 / U9.7, 73 -> 73.  A read-only corridor screen on the supplies-first candidate board closes the loop: NFC_XIN's missing join is opened by ripping up NFC_VDD_A alone and NFC_XOUT's by NFC_VDD_D alone.  The conflict is mutual and it is TINY -- 1.149 mm and 0.583 mm of route -- which is why no ordering and no containment-bounded eviction changes the total.",
  "framework_defect_found_and_fixed": "The first run of this batch closed both supplies and was REFUSED on FOUR real `items_not_allowed` reports: the rebuilt NFC_XOUT came back with 0.7211 mm and 1.3416 mm of track on In2.Cu and TWO F-to-B barrels.  `.kicad_dru` section 6 forbids both by name and `DRU_CLASS` carried `layers=None` for NFC_OSC, NFC_RF and NFC_RX.  Fixed by the USB_D recipe -- a single-layer contract makes the via inexpressible rather than merely illegal.  Re-run: ZERO attributable DRC.",
